# Agent / human workflow

## Roles (strict)

| Who | Does |
|-----|------|
| **Agent (this chat)** | Plans; **writes work into `docs/INSTRUCTIONS.md` and pushes** before the human runs it; short chat pointer only. On **check**: pull and review committed work. Builder/CDN verify only if explicitly requested at end of flow. |
| **Human** | **Everything operational:** Makou, discs, DuckStation, shell, **all** scripts, builds, commits, pushes, publish. |

No second agent on the disc/build machine.

## Hard rule: instructions live in the repo

**Never** give an operational task that only exists in chat.

Before asking the human to execute:

1. Write **`docs/INSTRUCTIONS.md`** (Goal, steps, COPY-PASTE, empty EVIDENCE) — or the matching skill's committed checklist if that is the runbook. Overwrite each run.
2. Prefer small **scripts** (`scripts/…`). Put the exact invoke line in COPY-PASTE.
3. **Commit + push** from the agent side.
4. Chat: one-line goal + "pull and open `docs/INSTRUCTIONS.md`" + **check**.

Agent must not: run CSR release scripts as the real publish path; expect local bins; paste-large-output-into-chat requests; "see the handoff".

## One atomic task per reply

Exactly one operational task per agent turn.

## `docs/INSTRUCTIONS.md` layout (markdown)

Real markdown: `# Task`, `## Goal`, `## Steps`, `## Copy-paste` (bash fence), `## Evidence` when executing work. Idle = short status + last ship note.

## Human loop

```bash
cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)"
git pull --ff-only
# STEPS / COPY-PASTE from docs/INSTRUCTIONS.md
git add docs/INSTRUCTIONS.md builder/ bases/   # as applicable
git commit -m "ops: <task>"
git push
```

Then say **check**. Never commit `.bin` / `.cue` / ISO.

## On "check"

Pull → review committed evidence/diff → next single task in-repo.
Not live builder/CDN unless explicitly requested.

Confirmed RE/playtest conclusions that belong in **Final-Fantasy-7-Modding** (addresses, watches, stub behavior) must be journaled there under `docs/findings/` the same turn — do not leave them only in chat (Modding rule `capture-research-findings`).

## Before agent acts

```bash
git pull --ff-only
```

Stop if pull fails.
